max-w-[60rem]"><p class=3D"self-stretch text-grey-8 text-base font-normal l=
eading-7"><strong>Scaling post-training is all we did for GLM-5.3.</strong>=
 With GLM-5.2 we built the stack: <a class=3D"hover:text-gray-500 underline=
" target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.12201">IndexShare</a=
> for efficient long-context processing, <a class=3D"hover:text-gray-500 un=
derline" target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.07508">SAO</a=
> for RL on long-horizon tasks, and <a class=3D"hover:text-gray-500 underli=
ne" target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://github.com/THUDM/slime">slime</a> for=
 large-scale asynchronous training =E2=80=94 all running on the long-horizo=
n task environments we have been accumulating. Over the past month we kept =
scaling on this stack: more environments, more diverse tasks, and more comp=
ute spent training on them.</p>
<p class=3D"self-stretch text-grey-8 text-base font-normal leading-7">Today=
 we are releasing GLM-5.3. It uses the same base model as GLM-5.2 =E2=80=94=
 every gain comes from post-training. Compared with GLM-5.2, it is much bet=
ter at complex coding and long-horizon tasks:</p>
<ul class=3D"list-disc pl-6">
<li><strong>Stronger Coding:</strong> GLM-5.3 is the most capable open-weig=
hts model for coding, with a 50% improvement over GLM-5.2 on our in-house Z=
.ai Code Bench. It also achieve open-source SOTA on public benchmarks inclu=
ding Terminal Bench 3.0 and Agents' Last Exam.</li>
<li><strong>Emergent Cyber Capability:</strong> As we scaled post-training,=
 cyber capability developed faster than we expected. GLM-5.3 is state of th=
e art on CyberGym for vulnerability discovery, and its gains are largest fu=
rther up the exploitation chain, where it more than doubles GLM-5.2 on expl=
oitation benchmarks.</li>
<li><strong>Open Source:</strong> We will release the weights in two weeks =
after launch, once safety evaluation and hardening are complete.</li>
</ul>
